  "timeframe": "N/A - current configuration state",
  "criteria": "For each distribution, check and report: (1) TLS - minimum TLS protocol version (ViewerCertificate.MinimumProtocolVersion), whether SSLSupportMethod is sni-only or vip, whether viewer protocol policy allows HTTP (redirect-to-https vs allow-all vs https-only) for each cache behavior; (2) WAF - whether WebACLId is set/non-empty; (3) Origin access - for S3 origins check if OriginAccessControl/OriginAccessIdentity is configured (vs public bucket access), for custom/ALB origins check OriginProtocolPolicy (http-only vs https-only) and OriginSslProtocols; (4) Caching - cache policy or forwarded headers/cookies/query strings settings, default TTL values, whether compression is enabled; (5) Logging - whether standard access logging (Logging.Enabled) is turned on and to which S3 bucket, also check if real-time logs are configured. Report findings as a structured list per distribution ID/domain name with the specific misconfiguration or good practice noted, flagging anything insecure or suboptimal clearly (e.g. missing WAF, TLSv1.0, HTTP allowed, logging disabled, no OAC)."
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit CloudFront distribution configs: TLS, WAF, origin access, caching, logging"}, {"id": "tooluse_L3jKtDRkqrj8R029OGSLSj", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Retrieve recent cost data for Amazon CloudFront in this AWS account to support an operational cost review.",
  "context": "User wants a cost dimension included in a CloudFront operational review, with findings rated by severity (e.g. unexpectedly high spend, inefficient pricing class, data transfer costs).",
  "resources": ["AWS Cost Explorer, CloudFront service costs, broken down by usage type if possible (e.g. data transfer out, requests, invalidations)"],
  "timeframe": "Last 3 months, monthly granularity, ending now (2026-10-21)",
  "criteria": "Report total CloudFront spend per month for the last 3 months, trend direction, and a breakdown by usage type (data transfer, requests, invalidations) if available. Flag anything notable: rising trend, unusually high invalidation costs, or disproportionate data transfer costs. Also note if any CloudFront distributions appear to use a non-default (more expensive) PriceClass if that data is accessible via CloudFront distribution configs."
}", "deep_research": false}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Pull CloudFront cost data from Cost Explorer for the review"}], "created_at": null}

